@startuml 06-seq-reconnect
!include _style.iuml
title Reconnecting after a drop: state-vector sync

participant "Peer\n(MUPPET)" as p
participant "Tracker\n(branch main)" as t

p -> t : update ops (1,1)…(1,40)
t --> p : others' ops
p -x t : connection drops
...
p -> p : keeps editing offline:\nops (1,41)…(1,55)
t -> t : meanwhile admits ops\nfrom other peers
...
p -> t : reconnect + authenticate
p -> t : sync-1: my state vector\n{1:55, 2:120, 3:8}
t -> p : sync-1: tracker's state vector\n{1:40, 2:131, 3:9}
t --> p : sync-2: ops you're missing\n(2,121…131), (3,9)
p --> t : sync-2: ops you're missing\n(1,41…55)
p -> p : integrate
t -> t : admit, record, fan out

note over p, t
  Both now at {1:55, 2:131, 3:9}.
  Ops are idempotent and order-free, so the transport
  only needs "eventually, at least once". No resume
  token, no archive query: the state vectors say it all.
end note
@enduml
